# LF everywhere, on Windows too (core.autocrlf would check text out as CRLF). The engine embeds
# and reads its data files (predict/, dict/, the test corpora) and the web playground serves them
# and its sample texts as they are; a \r in any of them is a character the macOS and Linux
# builds don't see. Nothing here needs CRLF: PowerShell, CMake and Inno Setup read LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.bin binary
*.wasm binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jar binary
